  "CardHelpSection": {
    "ParentObjectID": "advanced_copper_tools_copper_stove",
    "LocalizationKey": "Advanced_Copper_Tools_CopperStove_CardHelpSection",
    "DefaultText": "<b>Crafted:</b> In two stages: cast the stove top (small molten crucible, 2 mud bricks, 2 clay), then assemble it from 4 metal sheets of one metal, 4 copper nails and 1 tin solder. The stove is the metal of its sheets.\n\n<b>Uses:</b> Place in environment as a fireplace that holds 600 weight, like a campfire: one cooking pot or two clay bowls. Keeps its fuel and its metal when picked up, and gives Sanctuary while placed: +75 in copper or Tin Bronze, +80 in Ghost Bronze, +65 in Tin, +90 in White Bronze. Accepts oak wood, twigs, or charcoal as fuel. Also a component for the copper bathtub blueprint."
  },
